From: rhodep port <none@example.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 21:40:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm6375: add the APSS watchdog

SM6375 has the usual KPSS watchdog and mainline never described it, so
qcom-wdt has nothing to bind to: /sys/class/watchdog is empty and there
is no /dev/watchdog, even with CONFIG_QCOM_WDT=y.

Address and interrupt from the vendor tree, which puts it somewhere the
siblings do not -- SM6115 and QCM2290 use 0x0f017000, holi uses
0x0f410000:

	wdog: qcom,wdt@f410000 {
		compatible = "qcom,msm-watchdog";
		reg = <0xf410000 0x1000>;
		interrupts = <0 0 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>,
			     <0 1 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
		qcom,bark-time = <11000>;
		qcom,pet-time = <9360>;
	};

The first interrupt is the bark, which is what qcom-wdt wants; the second
is the bite and the driver has no use for it. Trigger type follows the
mainline siblings rather than the vendor's LEVEL_HIGH, matching how
sm6115.dtsi and agatti.dtsi describe the same signal.

Beyond describing hardware that exists, this is wanted for a specific
reason. The port has a reset that takes the whole SoC down a few seconds
after the modem attaches to LTE, silently: no CPU exception, no
backtrace, nothing from the softlockup detector, and a console recording
that simply stops. The bootloader reports it as
androidboot.bootreason=watchdog, and until now there was no way to see
anything before it, because nothing on the AP side was watching.

qcom-wdt supports the bark as a pretimeout, and match_data_kpss enables
it. With a pretimeout set and the panic governor selected, a bite that
would otherwise be silent is preceded by a panic with every CPU's
backtrace -- which, since the ramoops console now survives a reset, is
readable afterwards.

Signed-off-by: rhodep port <none@example.com>
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6375.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6375.dtsi
@@ -1803,6 +1803,13 @@
 			interrupt-controller;
 		};
 
+		watchdog@f410000 {
+			compatible = "qcom,apss-wdt-sm6375", "qcom,kpss-wdt";
+			reg = <0 0x0f410000 0 0x1000>;
+			clocks = <&sleep_clk>;
+			interrupts = <GIC_SPI 0 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>;
+		};
+
 		timer@f420000 {
 			compatible = "arm,armv7-timer-mem";
 			reg = <0 0x0f420000 0 0x1000>;
